(Abstract) Tj
T*
(Family members caring for patients with life-limiting illnesses experience substantial) Tj
T*
(psychological distress, anxiety, and demoralized mood. Structured creative activities may) Tj
T*
(offer accessible, low-cost approaches to enhance coping and emotional resilience. This) Tj
T*
(protocol describes a randomized controlled trial evaluating mandala-based artistic) Tj
T*
(engagement for family caregivers in palliative care settings. A total of 84 family members) Tj
T*
(will be randomly assigned 1:1 to either a 4-week mandala artistic engagement program or) Tj
T*
(standard care control. Intervention participants will complete one structured 1-hour) Tj
T*
(mandala drawing and coloring session weekly in a calm, dedicated space using provided) Tj
T*
(materials. Primary outcome measures include the Psychological Well-Being Scale) Tj
T*
(administered at baseline and 4 weeks. Secondary assessments encompass the Spiritual Well-) Tj
T*
(Being Scale and quality-of-life measures. We hypothesize that creative engagement will) Tj
T*
(enhance psychological well-being through mechanisms of mindful attention, self-expression,) Tj
T*
(and symbolic personal meaning-making during a period of existential challenge.) Tj
